# The World Atlas, second region.
#
# Five nodes docking onto the first region's outer edge, and only one of them changes anything on a
# board. That is not a shortage of ideas — it is what the balance had room for.
#
# The first region already grants three extra skips and three extra Pivot Tokens, which is the most
# AtlasPackTests allows and also where TokenRules.MaximumCapacity tops out, so a fourth of either
# would have to raise a ceiling that exists to stop a board becoming impossible to deadlock. It grants
# two extra Star Essence against a limit of three, so exactly one more is available. Everything else
# this region can offer has to leave a board alone.
#
# So it makes the atlas cheaper instead. A discount relic takes one essence off every node still to be
# bought, and this region is a road whose prices come down as it is walked: five nodes with a face
# value of 41, which cost 33 if bought in the cheapest order. Nothing here is a side-bet that might
# not pay — every discount is also a prerequisite, so the saving is the road's own toll coming down
# rather than a wager on how much is left to buy.
#
# The one decision is which of the two roots to take first. Pilgrim Road is cheaper, so buying it
# first makes Waystone cost five instead of six; the other order pays six and then three. One essence,
# for reading the numbers.
#
# Worldsend is the outer edge. A third region docks onto it by naming it, and its discount is worth
# nothing until one exists — which is stated on the node rather than hidden in it.

pack: biome2
docks: storm-eye,wayfarer-mark

# The two roots, one off each of the first region's outer nodes. Both cheap, both discounts, and the
# cheaper one first is worth one essence.
node: pilgrim-road cost 4 at 3,1 gives discount 1 needs storm-eye
node: waystone cost 6 at 2,2 gives discount 1 needs wayfarer-mark

# The join, and the region's only effect a board will notice: the third and last Star Essence relic
# the balance allows.
node: star-ledger cost 9 at 3,2 gives essence 1 needs pilgrim-road,waystone

# The road out. Long Survey pays for itself against Worldsend alone; Worldsend pays for itself against
# a region that has not shipped, and says so.
node: long-survey cost 10 at 4,1 gives discount 1 needs star-ledger
node: worldsend cost 12 at 3,3 gives discount 1 needs long-survey
